-- the journal of a change to the source (part of language-implementation-remainder). A change
-- records the new text, has it checked, and puts the old text back if it does not check; a
-- process stopped between the first and the last left the unchecked text in the source, read
-- again by every later change (2026-11-22: two statements whose checks did not end were left so,
-- and every write after them ran their checks). So the intent is written first: the old text,
-- then the path (the path present means the text is whole); it is forgotten when the change is
-- kept or put back; and the next action that takes the write lock, finding it, puts the old text
-- back before doing anything else
hy-intend : List Word → List Word → List Word → Proc W Unit
hy-intend st path old = bind (h-write (list-append st "/pending-text") old) (λ b → bind (h-write (list-append st "/pending-path") path) (λ b2 → ret unit))
